{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T10:26:54.175Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T10:26:54.175Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/contract_change","value":{"api":"Managed npm update checks: update_error, update_check_reason, update_check_timeout_ms and PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS","before":"An npm update lookup that ran out of its fixed 10-second budget reported npm_registry_lookup_failed, like an unavailable registry","after":"It reports npm_registry_lookup_timed_out with update_check_timeout_ms naming the budget, other failures still report npm_registry_lookup_failed, and PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS sets the budget (default 10000, clamped to 1000-120000)","migrate":"Match npm_registry_lookup_timed_out wherever npm_registry_lookup_failed is matched, and raise PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS for a slow registry or cold start"}}],"before_hash":"d2019230d2da59a2dbd095d73c8c51ce390fa34db35e6ab03d1b66b4ef0ebe2e","after_hash":"ab216b1a62d1a001214a258dc71126b6ccbd513a44cf99e91f89eb9279c5564b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"cbbb920c6b70d84afcb70fe06d180a719ea412b1493897d60acd8c9c78590067"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T10:27:13.785Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T10:27:13.785Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-18T10:27:13.785Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 (gpt-6.2-sol, xhigh, on f0cbdfc88). The update-check findings and how each was fixed:\n- P2: the timeout was inferred from execFile's rejection (killed, and not a maxBuffer overflow). A provider that handles SIGTERM and exits 0 would resolve with partial output. Fix: runBoundedUpdateQuery owns the deadline, a setTimeout that aborts the child through an AbortSignal. A lookup still running when the deadline passes is reported as *_timed_out even when the child then exits cleanly. isExecTimeout and execFile's timeout option are gone. A unit test makes the child exit 0 with partial output on abort.\n- P2: the behaviour change had no contract_change declaration. Fix: declared on pm-5kfzjh and pm-43p2c3.\n- P3: the summary always carried an update_check_timeout_ms key, as undefined. Fix: the refresh, the normalizer and the summary add the key only when a lookup timed out (withUpdateCheckTimeout, optionalTimeoutBudget). Tests assert the key is absent with not.toHaveProperty.\n- P3: the default-budget tests inherited a PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS exported by the shell. Fix: they stub it unset and restore it.\n- P3: the docs overstated GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0. Fix: git also runs with GCM_INTERACTIVE=never, and the docs say that another askpass program or credential helper that prompts can still hold the lookup until its budget runs out.\nAbort semantics on Windows: an execFile abort emits an error that destroys the child's stdio and settles at once. It does not wait for a grandchild still holding the pipe, which the timeout option did with shell: true."}]}],"before_hash":"ab216b1a62d1a001214a258dc71126b6ccbd513a44cf99e91f89eb9279c5564b","after_hash":"bc3f013fbf427c69a2738886bea13faeea38a8d38e676697659f413bc19a4bb9","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8fea0d06528299de324e9be69bcfe3e65d740cdd9ca0a8baef2c53633bfbe371"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T10:27:28.957Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T10:27:28.957Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-18T10:27:28.957Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implemented on branch feat/sdk-stable-consumer-classifications. runNpmUpdateQuery now runs under runBoundedUpdateQuery's explicit deadline. A lookup still running when the budget passes reports npm_registry_lookup_timed_out, and every other failure reports npm_registry_lookup_failed. checkNpmUpdate carries timeout_ms; the managed record and the extension summary carry it as update_check_timeout_ms, present only on a timeout. PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS sets the budget for both providers (resolveExtensionUpdateCheckTimeoutMs: integer ms, default 10000, clamped to 1000-120000, and the default for a value that is not finite). The GH-1747 integration test (extension-diagnostic-purity) gives registry-backed checks a 60 s budget, so a cold Windows npm start no longer fails it. It also proves the timeout path end to end: a local registry that answers after 3 s under a 1 s budget reports npm_registry_lookup_timed_out with update_check_timeout_ms 1000. The local run is green in 2.5 s.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"bc3f013fbf427c69a2738886bea13faeea38a8d38e676697659f413bc19a4bb9","after_hash":"49306dfa0c2a585263ae8fcd9c0654b92d00aec69bdd6352e15e138bbb88ff31","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"756eeef79070af1c5f6840133ff9ecbc989fe1e312a56b8b2df93623e023198c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T10:47:18.440Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-18T10:47:18.439Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2 (gpt-6.2-sol, xhigh, on fd842f55f). The update-check findings and how each was fixed:\n- P2: the AbortSignal deadline still waited for the pipes. Node drops the abort listener when the launcher exits, so a descendant holding stdout or stderr kept execFile pending; Codex measured 1.38 s for a 400 ms budget. Aborting also killed only the launcher. Fix: runBoundedUpdateQuery now uses spawn directly, because execFile does not forward detached. The child is spawned detached on POSIX (its own process group) with windowsHide, stdin ignored and stderr drained and discarded, and stdout is bounded by a per-provider maxBuffer (npm 64 KiB, git 1 MiB). The deadline settles the promise on its own, destroys the pipes and calls killProcessTree: SIGKILL to the process group on POSIX, taskkill /T /F on Windows. killProcessTree moved from src/sdk/test/execution.ts into src/core/shared/process-tree.ts so both callers share it. The new tests/integration/extensions/update-check-process-tree.integration.spec.ts (POSIX) runs a fake git that leaves sleep 30 on its pipes and exits 0. The check settles as github_remote_lookup_timed_out in about 1 s, and the descendant is gone within 5 s. On the round-1 design this test would wait the full 30 s.\n- P3: a stale stored update_check_timeout_ms survived normalization next to a non-timeout reason. Fix: the managed-state normalizer keeps it only beside npm_registry_lookup_timed_out or github_remote_lookup_timed_out. The codes are spelled locally because importing update-check would close a cycle through install-sources and bundled-catalog. Tests pin both codes and the drop cases."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T10:47:18.440Z"}],"before_hash":"49306dfa0c2a585263ae8fcd9c0654b92d00aec69bdd6352e15e138bbb88ff31","after_hash":"170d0e6e4e3468a80b1270be59cb145a2618a661729637b503b3d8a6dffd5dbf","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d11f8aa6dd3eb869a500588370e1ed048d8f2df2263f20dfd282ec7d8431aeb9"}
