{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T10:52:32.933Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-18T10:52:32.932Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1752 bot review, first pass: CodeRabbit on fd842f55f. The update-check findings and how each was handled:\n- Major (outside the diff): the deadline did not settle while a helper held the pipes. Already fixed in c564fc892 (spawn plus an independent deadline). The Minor about only the direct child being signalled was fixed in the same commit by the process-group or taskkill /T teardown, with a real fake-git integration test.\n- A stale stored budget passed normalization. Already fixed in c564fc892: the budget is kept only beside a timed-out reason.\n- The snapshot acknowledgement said only required mappings were affected. Fix: it now also names consumers that assert the exact keyof ManagedExtensionRecord key set.\n- The integration timeout scenario could pass before npm reached the registry, and three 60 s lookups did not fit the 120 s test timeout. Fix: the registry now holds the request unanswered, the budget is 8 s so a warm npm has time to reach it, the test asserts the held request arrived (heldRequests is 1), and the test timeout is 300 s.\n- Two unit assertions could pass if an entry were dropped. Fix: they now assert the offline refresh keeps both entries and normalization keeps the entry's identity.\n- Declined here, filed as pm-9x9drr: manage --fix-managed-state holds the extension state lock across the remote lookups. That predates this change, and default behaviour is unchanged. Fixing it means splitting the locked manage handler."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T10:52:32.933Z"}],"before_hash":"719ee495d202be852a63c439415565b77b3b5271481a760566e823526b92d6d4","after_hash":"3efb8dd381ab62548aaa45b1c85d4290291b2afc4b9c2db26aa44263798c7241","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a697d6a3958b68a789b112eee5756f6f3fb8429261258c1e0d999ae5e589f6d5"}
